WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.430
It's a debate that's raged among Star Wars
fans since time immemorial ... or at least

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.420
since the prequels came out.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.520
What's the right order to watch every Star
Wars movie?

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.360
Well, pour yourself a glass of blue milk and
settle in to watch every Star Wars movie in

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.360
the right order.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.280
If you're going to make the commitment to
watch every single Star Wars movie, there's

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.900
only one place you can logically start - and
it's not with Episode I.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.640
The first three Star Wars movies, commonly
referred to as the original trilogy, remain

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.860
the defining example of what Star Wars is
to this day.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.600
Almost everything that's iconic about the
franchise, from lightsabers and the Force

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.840
to droids and John Williams' score, was introduced
in the first Star Wars movie, A New Hope.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.500
Seriously, this film is what most people think
of when they hear the words "Star Wars," and

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.100
it remains one of the most iconic movies ever
made.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.440
By beginning your Star Wars journey with A
New Hope, which was originally just called

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:56.680
Star Wars, in case you needed further proof
of where to start, you're experiencing the

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.880
space saga in its purest form.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:04.080
The original trilogy was the only version
of Star Wars that existed for almost two decades,

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:08.180
and every film that's come since has been
loaded with references and callbacks to these

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:11.720
movies in a never ending quest to match their
reputation and status.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.750
And A New Hope alone introduces loads of some
of the most recognizable characters in cinema,

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:29.880
including Luke Skywalker, Princess Leia, Han
Solo, Chewbacca, C-3PO, R2-D2, Darth Vader,

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.160
and Obi-Wan Kenobi.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.700
The original trilogy is the definition of
Star Wars, and to fully comprehend the saga

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.520
you're about to undertake, you need to watch
A New Hope first.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.180
Since we've established you're starting your
Star Wars marathon with the original trilogy,

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.400
your next appointment is, of course, with
The Empire Strikes Back.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:53.120
As the direct sequel to A New Hope, the 1980
film - which is often lauded as the best in

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:58.090
the franchise - further builds on the characters
and story of its predecessor, while also introducing

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.580
some new franchise icons.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.620
Luke continues his Jedi training, working
his way up to an eventual confrontation with

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.560
Darth Vader.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:10.240
Yoda is introduced as Luke's new Jedi master
and instantly becomes a fan favorite.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.640
Boba Fett is also introduced as the bounty
hunter who hunts down Han Solo and freezes

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:16.480
him in carbonite.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:21.440
And Lando Calrissian shows up as well, the
only man in the galaxy who could actually

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.940
be cooler than Han Solo.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:27.950
The story developments in the film are also
notable, as the Empire gains strength by beating

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:33.340
the Rebels at every turn, a relationship blossoms
between Han and Leia, and Luke discovers that

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:37.200
Vader is his father in one of cinema's most
memorable twists.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.120
By following up A New Hope with The Empire
Strikes Back, you're seeing these iconic characters

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:47.020
grow, meeting more memorable Star Wars players,
and becoming emotionally invested in the story

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.700
as the Rebellion sees some major setbacks
in their fight against the Empire.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:56.200
The Empire Strikes Back may be the ideal Star
Wars movie, but it's also a sequel, and therefore

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.520
should be watched only after consuming its
predecessor.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:05.540
Return of the Jedi is up next, as it is - for
better or worse - the climax of the original

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.040
trilogy.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:11.100
The movie gets a lot of hate, especially from
modern audiences, for a few of its choices.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.460
A lot of people don't like that the film features
a new Death Star.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:19.280
Some aren't crazy about the fact that Han
Solo is brought back from his frozen state.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:22.150
And a lot of people really hate the Ewoks.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:26.970
The cute teddy bear aliens are viewed by some
as a bridge too far into Merchandise Town,

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:31.580
and their ability to defeat the Empire with
sticks and stones stretches credibility.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:35.860
However, Return of the Jedi really isn't as
bad as some would have you believe.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:41.270
With expanded roles for both Jabba the Hutt
and the Emperor, the film continues the original

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.800
trilogy's tradition of bringing in iconic
characters in every installment.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:49.820
It also adds another big twist in the reveal
that Luke and Leia are twins.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.760
And it features a ton of iconic scenes.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:57.380
There's the escape from Jabba's palace, complete
with the Sarlacc pit, the speeder bike chase

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.800
on Endor, and the redemption of Darth Vader.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.380
Even the Ewoks, hated as they are, were pretty
popular at the time the movie was released

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.940
and are iconic in their own right.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.780
So despite its flaws, Return of the Jedi makes
for a satisfying conclusion to the original

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:11.280
trilogy.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.760
There's no way around this, so we'll just
come right out and say it.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.100
The prequel movies aren't very good.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:22.870
They're loathed by many fans, and they don't
feel much at all like Star Wars, or at least

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.220
Star Wars as defined by the original trilogy.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:31.260
Those films told the saga of farm boy Luke
Skywalker, who becomes a powerful Jedi warrior,

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.780
discovers that the murderous Darth Vader is
his father, and then overthrows the Emperor.

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:36.540
Or just….

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:37.500
throws him.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:43.160
The prequels take place almost entirely prior
to Luke's birth and reveal how the Chosen

00:04:43.169 --> 00:04:48.889
One of the Jedi, Anakin Skywalker, becomes
Vader, the scourge of the galaxy and Palpatine's

00:04:48.889 --> 00:04:50.000
right-hand man.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:54.620
It's an interesting concept, but one that
the prequel movies don't pull off terribly

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.120
well.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:57.880
And it's especially bad in this first installment.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:03.580
The Phantom Menace is mainly remembered for
a few, let's say, misguided decisions.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:09.439
One is an over-reliance on CGI, which looks
incredibly dated today, while also somehow

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:12.280
worse than the original trilogy's practical
effects.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:17.560
Second is a heavy focus on the politics of
the Galactic Republic rather than action and

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.060
adventure.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:24.060
And third is Jar Jar Binks, the kid-friendly,
all-CGI character that everyone loves to hate.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:29.680
"Monsters out there, leaking in here, all
sinking and no power?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.280
When youssa thinking wessa in trouble?"

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:37.479
The Phantom Menace just doesn't feel like
Star Wars to many fans, but if you're determined

00:05:37.479 --> 00:05:41.339
to watch every movie in the franchise, you
might as well watch this one while the memory

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.980
of the original trilogy is still fresh in
your mind.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:48.660
Attack of the Clones seemed to hear the complaints
about The Phantom Menace and doubled down

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.600
on all of them.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:55.400
The second film in the prequel trilogy takes
the unrealistic CGI to cartoonish levels,

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.960
and it features even more boring senatorial
debates.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.160
But it gets worse.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:03.999
The film also replaces the villainous Darth
Maul, one of the only cool aspects of The

00:06:03.999 --> 00:06:08.370
Phantom Menace, with Count Dooku and a bunch
of non-threatening CGI soldiers that look

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:09.880
like they came out of an old video game.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:15.700
There's also a forced romance between Anakin
and his future wife Padme, and the pair probably

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.540
have less chemistry than any movie couple
ever.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.460
Pretty much the only good thing about Attack
of the Clones is that it features less Jar

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.140
Jar Binks than its predecessor.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.840
So why watch Attack of the Clones at all if
it's so terrible?

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:33.020
Well, it still advances the story of Anakin
Skywalker's eventual turn to the dark side,

00:06:33.029 --> 00:06:37.909
albeit clumsily, and the Clone Wars are a
pretty significant part of Star Wars lore,

00:06:37.909 --> 00:06:39.900
so it doesn't hurt to see what kicked them
off.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:44.960
It may be a slog to get through, and it's
nowhere near as entertaining as the original

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.740
trilogy, but Attack of the Clones is still
a part of the Star Wars story, and it should

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.599
be watched right after The Phantom Menace.

00:06:51.719 --> 00:06:55.559
After watching the first two prequels, you
may be wondering just what you've gotten yourself

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.200
into.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:01.219
That's why we recommend taking a brief respite
from the prequels to remind yourself why you're

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.560
sitting through them to begin with, and that
reason is Darth Vader.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:09.530
The prequels, awkward as they may be, are
all about Anakin's transformation into the

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:10.320
Sith Lord.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:14.259
It's easy to forget that while watching the
first two episodes, which is why you should

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:17.900
follow up Attack of the Clones with Rogue
One: A Star Wars Story.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:22.930
The movie is the darkest of all Star Wars
films, as the bulk of its characters don't

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.540
survive past the final scene.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.420
In other words, this isn't the start of a
new trilogy.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.559
The story takes place right before A New Hope,
and it centers on the group of Rebel spies

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.540
who steal the plans to the Death Star immediately
prior to the start of that film.

00:07:37.249 --> 00:07:41.480
So given the time period in which Rogue One
takes place, that means we get Darth Vader

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:44.159
at the full height of his powers and villainy.

00:07:44.159 --> 00:07:48.409
With modern effects, Vader is transformed
into a more frightening and impressive presence

00:07:48.409 --> 00:07:49.060
than ever.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:54.400
Watching him slaughter a bunch of Rebel soldiers
will remind you of why you're watching the

00:07:54.409 --> 00:07:58.129
prequels, and it may even get you excited
to watch the final prequel movie so you can

00:07:58.129 --> 00:07:59.120
witness his origin.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:03.440
Congratulations, you've made it to the final
prequel movie!

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:07.120
The good news is that it's considerably better
than the previous two prequel films.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.720
The bad news is that it's still not great.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:15.630
Revenge of the Sith finally gives us the evil
Anakin Skywalker we've been waiting for, and

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:20.469
while there are still issues with bad CGI,
horrible dialogue, and a few iffy performances…

00:08:20.469 --> 00:08:22.700
It at least tells a pretty compelling story.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:27.520
Anakin fully turns to the dark side of the
Force, taking on the identity of Darth Vader

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.539
and doing all sorts of horrible things.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:34.920
He kills a bunch of kids, Force chokes his
pregnant wife, and is just an all-around evil

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:35.420
dude.

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:41.020
And frankly, evil Anakin is way more interesting
than pod racing Anakin, lovesick Anakin, or

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.260
any of the other Anakins who've popped up
in the earlier prequels.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:49.640
Plus, near the end of Episode III, Anakin
completes his transformation into full-on

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:53.520
Darth Vader with the suit and everything,
and it's admittedly pretty cool.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:58.800
The transformation occurs after Anakin is
rebuilt following a lightsaber duel with Obi-Wan

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:03.000
that left him severely debilitated, which
gives some nice emotional weight to the scene.

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:08.080
And once you see Anakin put on that iconic
Vader mask for the first time, you'll instantly

00:09:08.089 --> 00:09:12.779
flashback to visions of Vader being menacing
and awesome in the original trilogy and Rogue

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:13.280
One.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.520
And for a brief shining moment, sitting through
the entire prequel trilogy will have seemed

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:18.180
worth it.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:23.520
By this point, it's been an epic four movies
since you've seen any of the "big three" characters

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:28.500
from the original trilogy, not counting the
baby Luke and baby Leia cameos in Revenge

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.020
of the Sith.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:33.959
With a total of seven films in the bag, you've
now watched more movies without Han Solo than

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:39.920
with him, so it's time to rectify that unpleasant
situation by screening Solo: A Star Wars Story.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:44.840
The 2018 film may have a bad reputation, but
it's one that isn't wholly deserved.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:50.120
The film's infamous director shakeup, its
casting of an actor not named Harrison Ford

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:54.940
to play Han, and its premiere taking place
only five months after the divisive The Last

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:59.620
Jedi all led to an underwhelming box office
take and tepid critical response.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:05.100
Solo's lackluster performance caused Disney
to rethink its strategy with Star Wars movies,

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.810
which has resulted in a break from standalone
movies.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:11.690
But despite its controversy and failure to
leave a significant mark on the Star Wars

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:15.000
universe, Solo actually makes for a pretty
fun watch.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:19.140
Don't get us wrong, it's not a great film
by any means, and there's certainly nothing

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.400
revolutionary about it.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:24.760
It's a mostly by-the-numbers adventure set
in the Star Wars universe that features some

00:10:24.769 --> 00:10:29.110
new interpretations of old characters, of
which Donald Glover's Lando in particular

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:33.900
is a highlight, some cool alien creatures,
and lots of fun fan service.

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:38.740
Also, watching Solo now and getting reacquainted
with Han makes his storyline that much more

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.620
poignant in the next film on the list.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:46.500
Only time will tell just how iconic the sequel
trilogy of Star Wars films will end up being,

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:50.200
but there's no denying their success, especially
The Force Awakens.

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:55.639
The first Star Wars movie to be released by
Disney grossed over $2 billion worldwide,

00:10:55.640 --> 00:11:02.400
and it remains the highest-earner of all time
domestically with a $936 million take.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.699
The film brought back almost every character
of note from the original trilogy, making

00:11:06.699 --> 00:11:10.690
sure that anyone burned by the prequels' weirdness
would be treated with a heavy dose of the

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.160
Star Wars they remembered.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.880
"I got a bad feeling about this."

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:17.160
Leia commanding Rebel Resistance forces?

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:17.900
Check.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.200
Han and Chewie flying the Millennium Falcon?

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:20.940
Check.

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:23.300
Luke Skywalker… making an appearance?

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:24.100
Check.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:29.060
The Force Awakens also introduced a variety
of new characters, and though the fan bases

00:11:29.069 --> 00:11:34.009
dedicated to Rey, Finn, Poe, and Kylo Ren
may not quite match the fervor attached to

00:11:34.009 --> 00:11:38.870
their original trilogy parallels, the characters
are now undeniably a big part of the Star

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:39.540
Wars story.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:44.220
If you find yourself really missing the original
trilogy after watching the prequels, then

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:48.600
you should especially enjoy The Force Awakens
because it basically retells the story of

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.260
A New Hope.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:54.000
A nobody finds out she can use the Force and
joins up with a group of rebels to fight a

00:11:54.001 --> 00:11:58.310
guy in a black helmet so they can stop him
and his evil empire from using a superweapon

00:11:58.310 --> 00:11:59.540
that can blow up planets.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:02.880
It may not be original, but it's definitely
Star Wars.

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:07.520
The Last Jedi is possibly the strangest Star
Wars movie ever.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:12.060
The sequel to The Force Awakens doesn't really
build on any of the threads that were started

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.280
by its predecessor.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.740
Who are Rey's parents?

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:15.700
Doesn't matter.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:16.540
Who is Snoke?

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:17.520
Doesn't matter.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:21.440
Didn't Finn already have a character arc where
he learned to be brave and commit himself

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.580
to a greater good?

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.860
Doesn't matter, he's doing it again.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:29.379
The Last Jedi almost seems to purposely undo
pretty much every decision that was made in

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:30.380
The Force Awakens.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.260
"I thought I'd find answers here.

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:35.240
I was wrong."

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:40.120
And while some thought this kind of shakeup
was the exact kind of bold thinking the franchise

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:44.020
needed, others thought it was poor storytelling
and a disservice to the fans.

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:49.920
This dichotomy has led to the film being labeled
as the most divisive in the Star Wars canon.

00:12:49.939 --> 00:12:54.410
The Last Jedi is so jarringly different from
other Star Wars movies that it almost feels

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:57.940
as if you could watch it anywhere in this
sequence and it wouldn't matter, but since

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.640
it's the sequel to The Force Awakens, we're
placing it here.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:06.060
Though it's true that the movie doesn't seem
to have much respect for its predecessor,

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:09.980
it does still move the Skywalker saga along
in a few important ways.

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:15.400
Rey and Kylo Ren both grow, with her becoming
a Jedi and him becoming the new supreme leader

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.240
of the First Order.

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:20.920
The pair also develop a weird sort of Force
connection that ends up forming the backbone

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.140
of this sequel trilogy.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.959
The sequel trilogy is strange.

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:29.420
Where The Last Jedi undid pretty much everything
in The Force Awakens, The Rise of Skywalker

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:32.000
undoes pretty much everything in The Last
Jedi.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:37.000
It turns out Rey is actually Emperor Palpatine's
granddaughter, Snoke was created and controlled

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:41.800
by Palpatine, and Finn... well, Finn still
doesn't really do very much.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:47.220
The movie seeks to satiate fans by giving
them the most Star Wars-y Star Wars movie

00:13:47.230 --> 00:13:51.610
ever, with more lightsaber fights, more classic
characters, and more planet-destroying weapons

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:52.340
than they can handle.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:57.200
While critics were unkind to the film, the
response from fans has been more positive,

00:13:57.200 --> 00:14:00.800
and no one can accuse The Rise of Skywalker
of being boring.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:07.540
The film gives a satisfying end to the Skywalker
story with Kylo Ren-slash-Ben Solo's redemption,

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:12.430
and by bringing back the Emperor - the main
villain of both previous trilogies - it does

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:14.960
make all three trilogies feel more connected.

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:19.300
Although it may not be the sequel trilogy
that George Lucas had planned or even wanted,

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:22.320
it's probably closer to what many fans wanted.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:27.380
The sequel trilogy wraps up and puts a bow
on most of what we've seen from big-screen

00:14:27.389 --> 00:14:31.259
Star Wars up to this point, which is why it
makes sense to end your movie journey with

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:31.760
this film.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:36.680
Love it or hate it, this is the end of the
Skywalker saga that has defined the franchise

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.240
for over 40 years.

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:41.020
Of course, this isn't the end of Star Wars.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:45.240
The Mandalorian is many things, but a movie
isn't one of them.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:46.620
So why include it here?

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:51.340
Because the series represents the future of
Star Wars, and the next Star Wars movies are

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:55.839
probably going to look a lot more like The
Mandalorian than anything that's come before.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:15:01.100
Plus, as the first-ever live-action Star Wars
TV show, its eight-episode first season had

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:06.399
a blockbuster feature film budget and as much
content as at least two movies, so comparing

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:09.329
it to a film isn't as outrageous as it seems.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:11.000
"This is the way."

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:12.900
"This is the way."

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:15.960
"This is the way."

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.740
Ever since the original trilogy, Star Wars
movies have been about the past.

00:15:21.749 --> 00:15:26.999
The prequel movies tell the story of young
Anakin Skywalker, Rogue One and Solo are both

00:15:26.999 --> 00:15:31.640
prequel stories based on A New Hope characters
and concepts, and the sequel trilogy is more

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:35.649
concerned with wrapping up the storylines
of the original trilogy's characters than

00:15:35.649 --> 00:15:37.300
it is with charting its own course.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.400
But that's not true for The Mandalorian.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:43.820
While there are certainly plenty of Star Wars
Easter eggs for fans to drool over, they're

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.570
hardly central to the story.

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:51.399
It's the first standalone Star Wars tale that
truly feels standalone, and its lack of connections

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:55.200
to the Skywalker saga shows a path forward
for the entire franchise.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:16:00.480
No longer bound by decades-old stories and
trilogy formats, Star Wars is now free to

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:04.000
finally explore more of the galaxy far, far
away.

